-
-The featured image was made with AI, haha.
-It came from a prompt along the lines of "a white building along a shopping arcade, a happy and comfortable share house life for university students."
-
-So, before graduating high school and heading off to university, you need to get ready to start living in a new environment. This is especially true if you're moving to a new city for college — finding a place to live can be a big challenge. Kobe is a popular city for students, thanks to its proximity to university campuses and lively downtown areas. This time, we'll introduce why a share house is a great option when searching for a room in Kobe.
-
-The benefits of living in a share house
-
-A share house is a home where multiple people live together. Not only is it more affordable than living alone, but you can also look forward to interactions in shared spaces and new encounters through communal living.
-
-1\. Save on rent
-
-Living in a share house lets you save money on rent compared to living alone. In Kobe especially, rent for a solo apartment can be quite high, which can be a real burden for students. By sharing common spaces efficiently, a share house helps cut down on rent.
-
-2. More chances to meet new people
-
-Because multiple people live together in a share house, there are plenty of opportunities to meet new people. Through interactions in shared spaces and everyday communal living, you can find like-minded friends. Share houses also come in many different styles, so you can live alongside people who share your hobbies and lifestyle.
-
-3\. A chance to build life skills through communal living
-
-Share houses have rules for living together. Following those rules while being considerate of others helps you develop communication and coordination skills, as well as the ability to cooperate — all things you naturally pick up through shared living. And by following the rules yourself and helping things run smoothly, you also build the kind of manners and etiquette that will serve you well as a member of society.
-
-Life in a share house in Kobe
-
-Kobe is home to many different share houses. Alongside students attending universities in the city, many international students and working holiday visitors also call these houses home. Depending on the house, you'll find events for practicing Japanese and plenty of international exchange, creating a wonderfully diverse community.
-
-1\. Convenient access around Kobe
-
-Kobe has many universities, as well as lively areas like Sannomiya and Motomachi that are especially appealing to students. Share houses are often located in spots with easy access to these areas, making them very attractive for student life.
-
-2\. Communication through communal living
-
-Living in a share house means new encounters and interactions are part of everyday life. Share houses also have common spaces, so you get to use a kitchen and living room you might not otherwise have access to. That gives you the chance to cook together or just chat with your housemates. Through communal living, friendships among students deepen, bringing new discoveries and fresh inspiration.
-
-In summary
-
-Kobe is a popular city to search for a room in, thanks to its proximity to university campuses and downtown areas. Living in a share house in particular can help you save on rent, meet new people, and build valuable life skills through communal living. With so many different share houses throughout Kobe, there's something appealing for every student. Why not give share house living a try?
-
